    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4887" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balnĕārĭs</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		balneum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to a bath</i>
			(post-Aug. for the foll.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argentum,</span>”
				<i>silver utensils used in baths</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 2, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jocus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Spart. Had. 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex. Sev. 42</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balnĕā-rĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>bathing utensils</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p.
				134, 36</span></i>.</div>
